      "created": 1784871962,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The MedCP live database and resource listing are unavailable here, so I can’t compute “most frequently used here” from local EHR counts in this session. If you want, I can proceed from the benchmark workspace files, but I’d need filesystem access/developer extension enabled; with only MedCP available, the honest answer is that the required site-specific frequency query cannot be completed.\nI can’t determine the most frequently used local RA immune-pathway drug classes from MedCP in this session because the MedCP clinical database connection failed and no MedCP resources were exposed to inspect.\n\nTo answer correctly, I would need counts of RA patients’ medication exposures joined to KG pathway-defined classes. Likely classes to rank would include TNF inhibitors, IL-6 pathway inhibitors, JAK inhibitors, T-cell costimulation modulators, B-cell depletion, and conventional DMARDs, but their local frequency cannot be inferred without the EHR query."
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
